    "vantier_2": {
      "type": "basic-content-helper-text-centered-full-width",
      "settings": {
        "kicker": "The proposition",
        "title": "A considered wardrobe with presence.",
        "body": "<p>We describe a neckline, a pleat or a contrast rather than claiming perfection. A one-shoulder midi is described by its diagonal drape and right side slit, a suit jacket by its defined shoulder and familiar proportions.</p><p>Looks come first. Pieces are designed to coordinate across edits, so a sculpted top can meet a wide-leg trouser and a navy jacket can meet its matching trouser, each chosen on its own.</p><p>VANTIER is a demonstration concept. There is no atelier history, no certification and no celebrity endorsement here, only sixty designs and the words that describe them.</p><p><a href=\"/pages/vantier-fit-guide\">Read the Fit Guide</a> &nbsp; <a href=\"/pages/vantier-client-services\">How we describe a design</a></p>",
        "alignment": "left",
        "max_width": "default",
